1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,240
At some point, your Python loop stops being fast enough.

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,840
Not theoretically, you will feel it.

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:12,440
You will run a calculation on 100,000 rows, and your laptop fan will spin up, and you

4
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:16,200
will sit there watching a cursor blink for 12 seconds.

5
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:21,440
Waiting for one number, a number you could have had in 0.08 seconds, if you would have

6
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:23,840
known one thing sooner.

7
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:27,280
Python loops are slow, numpy arrays are not.

8
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:32,280
So real two taught you to think in less than dictionaries, and that's real Python.

9
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:37,800
When data scientists say Python is fast, they don't mean the Python you have been writing.
